[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Document" load_steps=2 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/core/document.gd" id="1_doc"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_doc")
id = &"d16_cam_notes"
title = "C-2 cams — cutting notes"
byline = "pencil on the back of a parts envelope, 1966"
hand = 1
body = "CLOCK C-2. 24 HR DRUM. 3 CHANNELS.

CAM BLANK IS 12 TOOTH. DRUM IS 24 HR.
SO ONE TOOTH = TWO HOURS. NOT ONE.
CUT IT FOR ONE AND YOU GET HALF A DAY.

TOOTH N COVERS HOUR 2N AND 2N+1.

    TOOTH 0  -> 00 AND 01
    TOOTH 3  -> 06 AND 07
    TOOTH 7  -> 14 AND 15
    TOOTH 11 -> 22 AND 23

WORKED: DR K WANTS CH B LIT 0600.
        0600 / 2 = 3. CUT TOOTH 3.
        CHECKED ON THE BENCH. GOOD.

DRUM READS THE HOUR IT THINKS IT IS.
IT IS NOT A CLOCK. IT DOES NOT KNOW.
IF THE DRUM SAYS 0600 THE LAMP DOES
0600 WHATEVER THE TIME IS OUTSIDE.

CH A CAM IS SEIZED. LEFT IT. DR K SAYS
A IS NOT IN USE THIS RUN.

                              E.O."
